==English==

===Etymology===
Onomatopoeic; compare Japanese {{m|ja|フワフワ||lightly, softly|tr=fuwafuwa}}, Hungarian {{m|hu|puha}} (“soft, fluffy”), Polish {{m|pl|puchaty}} (“soft, fluffy”).  Alternatively, a variant of {{l|en|floow}}, possibly from {{etyl|vls|en}} {{m|vls|vluwe}}, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|velu}}, ultimately from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|villus}} ("shaggy hair, tuft of hair").

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/flʌf/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌf|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Anything [[light]], [[soft]] or [[fuzzy]], especially [[fur]], [[hair]], [[feather]]s.
# Anything [[inconsequential]] or [[superficial]].
#: {{ux|en|That article was basically a bunch of '''fluff'''. It didn't say anything substantive.}}
# [[lapse|Lapse]], especially a [[mistake]] in an [[actor]]’s [[line]]s.
# {{lb|en|New England}} [[marshmallow creme|Marshmallow creme]].
# {{lb|en|LGBT}} A [[passive]] partner in a [[lesbian]] relationship.
# {{lb|en|Australia|euphemistic}} A [[fart]].

{{rfex}}

